1
00:00:21,291 --> 00:00:24,581
TROLL

2
00:00:24,751 --> 00:00:26,921
There are no major changes.

3
00:00:27,251 --> 00:00:29,671
You will be compensated
with five pounds of gold.

4
00:00:29,751 --> 00:00:32,341
I will only pay you in exchange for his dead body.

5
00:00:34,881 --> 00:00:38,011
You can do whatever you want with their ship
and their cargo.

6
00:00:39,561 --> 00:00:41,221
Kill Thors.

7
00:00:42,891 --> 00:00:45,901
-Go ahead, boy.
-My turn next.

8
00:00:45,981 --> 00:00:47,561
Thors?

9
00:00:48,271 --> 00:00:50,231
The Troll of Jom.

10
00:00:50,321 --> 00:00:51,981
I've heard of him before.

11
00:00:52,071 --> 00:00:55,701
Are you sure it's okay if I kill him?
He's a hero to you guys.

12
00:00:57,531 --> 00:01:00,031
If he were a hero, I wouldn't have told you to kill him.

13
00:01:00,121 --> 00:01:02,831
He broke military law.

14
00:01:02,911 --> 00:01:04,461
He deserted during battle.

15
00:01:04,541 --> 00:01:08,171
Orders to have him executed were issued
15 years ago.

16
00:01:10,381 --> 00:01:15,341
I know you have strict laws,
but it's been 15 years.

17
00:01:17,221 --> 00:01:18,301
Thanks.

18
00:01:22,261 --> 00:01:23,811
No, don't get the wrong idea.

19
00:01:23,891 --> 00:01:27,231
As long as I receive fair payment,

20
00:01:27,311 --> 00:01:28,771
I'll do any job.

21
00:01:28,851 --> 00:01:31,021
But you know, master...

22
00:01:31,111 --> 00:01:35,651
If you're going to execute one of your own,
one of your own should kill him.

23
00:01:36,701 --> 00:01:39,071
You went to Iceland, right?

24
00:01:39,571 --> 00:01:41,871
Why didn't you kill him there?

25
00:01:43,791 --> 00:01:46,001
This Christian monk is dead.

26
00:01:47,081 --> 00:01:49,581
It's none of your business.

27
00:01:50,001 --> 00:01:53,211
You shouldn't ask questions.
It's for your own good.

28
00:01:55,591 --> 00:01:57,131
Well, all right.

29
00:01:57,511 --> 00:01:59,801
Five extra pounds of gold, paid in advance.

30
00:01:59,891 --> 00:02:01,221
Then I'll accept your job.

31
00:02:06,681 --> 00:02:11,191
You think you have the upper hand on me.
You must be confident in yourself.

32
00:02:21,321 --> 00:02:23,371
Oops, sorry.

33
00:02:23,911 --> 00:02:27,201
It slipped. Are you okay?

34
00:02:27,291 --> 00:02:29,501
Hey. Be careful.

35
00:02:29,581 --> 00:02:32,001
You guys almost hit me.

36
00:02:32,081 --> 00:02:33,211
You klutz.

37
00:02:33,291 --> 00:02:35,001
You drank too much.

38
00:02:36,261 --> 00:02:39,131
Five extra pounds of gold, paid in advance.

39
00:02:39,551 --> 00:02:41,341
You accept?

40
00:02:46,181 --> 00:02:47,351
All right.

41
00:02:49,641 --> 00:02:53,611
Excellent, master.
You're a great man. See you later.

42
00:02:54,821 --> 00:02:56,481
And by the way...

43
00:02:57,401 --> 00:03:00,491
What kind of a warrior is Thors?

44
00:03:00,571 --> 00:03:03,531
What does he look like? How does he fight?

45
00:03:06,291 --> 00:03:09,751
Thors is no longer a warrior.

46
00:03:14,461 --> 00:03:16,631
Okay. That's enough drinking.

47
00:03:16,711 --> 00:03:19,381
It's time to work, you bastards.

48
00:03:19,971 --> 00:03:22,181
Bjorn. Nice spear throw.

49
00:03:22,261 --> 00:03:23,261
No sweat.

50
00:03:23,721 --> 00:03:26,391
Even Floki was in shock.

51
00:03:26,471 --> 00:03:28,561
I wish I could have seen it myself.

52
00:03:34,981 --> 00:03:37,321
It seems he's not a man of empty words.

53
00:05:16,041 --> 00:05:20,001
The time has come for me,
Ari, son of Geitr, to become a man.

54
00:05:20,461 --> 00:05:24,381
I know. Don't say a word.
It will not be an easy journey.

55
00:05:25,051 --> 00:05:28,761
There's no guarantee that I won't be injured in battle.

56
00:05:29,091 --> 00:05:31,101
But I shall return.

57
00:05:31,181 --> 00:05:35,981
I'll return with a necklace
I seized from England as a gift to you.

58
00:05:36,061 --> 00:05:38,731
-And then will you...?
-Hey, I'm still sleepy.

59
00:05:39,311 --> 00:05:41,611
Ma-- Marry...

60
00:05:41,691 --> 00:05:42,731
Ari.

61
00:05:43,481 --> 00:05:46,741
You forgot your lunch.

62
00:05:46,821 --> 00:05:47,651
Mom?

63
00:05:47,741 --> 00:05:50,991
Why are you so careless?

64
00:05:51,081 --> 00:05:53,911
Make sure you share the salted herring
with everyone else.

65
00:05:53,991 --> 00:05:55,871
-I stuffed it full.
-Mom. Wait over there.

66
00:05:55,951 --> 00:05:58,331
How can you say that to your own mother?

67
00:05:58,421 --> 00:06:00,001
-When I return...
-What's wrong...?

68
00:06:00,081 --> 00:06:02,131
I'll finish what I was saying.
Wait for me, Ylva.

69
00:06:09,051 --> 00:06:12,011
They're departing today.

70
00:06:12,681 --> 00:06:14,971
I hope they don't die.

71
00:06:15,351 --> 00:06:16,521
Ylva.

72
00:06:16,601 --> 00:06:18,351
Do you have a moment?

73
00:06:18,441 --> 00:06:19,811
Wait. I'm first.

74
00:06:19,901 --> 00:06:21,611
Hey. Ylva.

75
00:06:22,021 --> 00:06:23,521
Can you try somewhere else?

76
00:06:29,031 --> 00:06:32,371
Make sure you bathe on Saturday, my boy.

77
00:06:32,451 --> 00:06:33,661
I know, Mom.

78
00:06:34,031 --> 00:06:35,491
I swear on my father's ax.

79
00:06:35,581 --> 00:06:38,251
I shall bring back a barrel full of gold coins.

80
00:06:39,121 --> 00:06:41,671
They're so excited.

81
00:06:41,751 --> 00:06:45,461
But there's only five of them in total.
That's not enough.

82
00:06:45,551 --> 00:06:48,131
Thors says that five is enough.

83
00:06:49,471 --> 00:06:52,011
Well, if that's what he says.

84
00:06:52,091 --> 00:06:56,851
But that's barely enough
for sailing two ships.

85
00:06:56,931 --> 00:07:00,941
It's Thors we're talking about.
I'm sure he has a reason.

86
00:07:01,601 --> 00:07:04,691
Hey. What were you talking about with Ylva just now?

87
00:07:04,771 --> 00:07:07,691
Shut up, you jackass. You stay away from her.

88
00:07:08,361 --> 00:07:10,781
Watch your back on the battlefield.

89
00:07:10,861 --> 00:07:13,571
Don't underestimate me.
I was going to say the same thing to you.

90
00:07:14,031 --> 00:07:15,781
-Ari.
-What?

91
00:07:20,001 --> 00:07:21,291
Be careful.

92
00:07:24,381 --> 00:07:25,881
You didn't finish.

93
00:07:25,961 --> 00:07:27,251
What did you say?

94
00:07:27,341 --> 00:07:29,171
This way.

95
00:07:29,801 --> 00:07:30,801
Miss.

96
00:07:32,131 --> 00:07:33,681
Are you worried about Ari?

97
00:07:34,511 --> 00:07:37,681
Want me to tell you a secret?

98
00:07:39,271 --> 00:07:41,691
What? They're not going to battle?

99
00:07:43,231 --> 00:07:44,561
It's a secret.

100
00:07:45,361 --> 00:07:49,111
We're going to stop by Norway
on our way to Jomsborg.

101
00:07:49,191 --> 00:07:53,701
Thors plans to leave the young men behind there.

102
00:07:54,281 --> 00:07:58,741
Thors is going to get some help
from some sailors in Norway

103
00:07:58,831 --> 00:08:00,581
to make it to Jomsborg.

104
00:08:00,911 --> 00:08:04,711
I'm friends with the previous King of Norway.

105
00:08:04,921 --> 00:08:06,711
I have a lot of influence there.

106
00:08:07,041 --> 00:08:10,171
As soon as I'm done with my business,

107
00:08:10,261 --> 00:08:12,341
I'll bring the young men back here.

108
00:08:14,181 --> 00:08:18,351
Five men is the most I can bring back
on my run-down ship.

109
00:08:19,061 --> 00:08:22,521
He won't bring anyone to the battlefield.

110
00:08:23,851 --> 00:08:26,731
That's the kind of person that Thors is.

111
00:08:31,241 --> 00:08:32,241
Thorfinn.

112
00:08:33,571 --> 00:08:35,911
Hey. Where are you?

113
00:08:36,451 --> 00:08:38,081
Thorfinn.

114
00:08:42,911 --> 00:08:44,671
Excuse me, Leif...

115
00:08:45,711 --> 00:08:50,421
Does that mean Thors is going
to the battlefield alone?

116
00:08:54,721 --> 00:08:56,641
Ready to row?

117
00:08:57,181 --> 00:08:58,471
Yeah.

118
00:09:05,851 --> 00:09:07,771
What's wrong with his oar?

119
00:09:08,231 --> 00:09:12,071
I can't believe Thorfinn isn't seeing Father off.

120
00:09:12,571 --> 00:09:15,531
I bet he's still angry he got scolded yesterday.

121
00:09:16,071 --> 00:09:17,781
-Helga.
-Yes?

122
00:09:18,871 --> 00:09:20,411
Tell Thorfinn...

123
00:09:22,621 --> 00:09:23,621
Well...

124
00:09:25,291 --> 00:09:26,291
What I mean is...

125
00:09:29,331 --> 00:09:31,671
Yes. I'll tell him.

126
00:09:35,301 --> 00:09:36,171
I'm counting on you.

127
00:09:38,301 --> 00:09:40,681
All right. Depart.

128
00:09:52,651 --> 00:09:53,781
He's so strong.

129
00:09:53,861 --> 00:09:55,491
Idiot. Don't stop rowing.

130
00:09:55,901 --> 00:09:57,111
Row. Row.

131
00:10:02,081 --> 00:10:04,491
You can do it.

132
00:10:04,581 --> 00:10:07,001
Bring home some souvenirs.

133
00:10:07,081 --> 00:10:09,711
See you.

134
00:10:13,591 --> 00:10:15,671
Raise the sail.

135
00:10:25,971 --> 00:10:27,431
My hands are peeling.

136
00:10:27,521 --> 00:10:29,061
My butt. My butt.

137
00:10:30,601 --> 00:10:32,061
Hey. Hang in there.

138
00:10:33,151 --> 00:10:34,731
Ari. Take the rudder.

139
00:10:36,031 --> 00:10:40,321
Mord and Magni, adjust the mainsheet.
Hakon and Grim, take the jib sheet.

140
00:10:41,821 --> 00:10:42,991
Are you tired?

141
00:10:44,031 --> 00:10:46,161
No. It's nothing.

142
00:10:48,751 --> 00:10:51,671
Don't worry.
We don't have to row any more for a while.

143
00:10:52,331 --> 00:10:55,631
We're riding the current now.
The ship will move on its own.

144
00:10:55,711 --> 00:10:59,011
Does that mean we can't turn back anymore, Father?

145
00:10:59,091 --> 00:11:00,511
Yeah, that's right.

146
00:11:02,141 --> 00:11:02,971
"Father"?

147
00:11:07,271 --> 00:11:08,271
Thor--?

148
00:11:08,351 --> 00:11:09,851
Thorfinn? You...

149
00:11:09,941 --> 00:11:11,271
You can tell me later.

150
00:11:16,021 --> 00:11:17,941
I made it...

151
00:11:30,001 --> 00:11:31,831
You naughty--

152
00:11:31,921 --> 00:11:32,921
Father.

153
00:11:34,171 --> 00:11:35,171
It's the ocean.

154
00:11:49,021 --> 00:11:51,691
This job is suspicious.

155
00:11:52,811 --> 00:11:53,941
Why?

156
00:11:54,021 --> 00:11:57,771
Floki is hiding too many secrets.

157
00:11:58,281 --> 00:12:00,821
He's lying about the execution order for Thors.

158
00:12:00,901 --> 00:12:02,701
I'm almost certain of it.

159
00:12:02,781 --> 00:12:03,611
Then why...?

160
00:12:04,951 --> 00:12:06,701
It's an assassination.

161
00:12:07,031 --> 00:12:10,871
Maybe it's a personal grudge or something.
But I'm sure he cooked this up all on his own.

162
00:12:10,951 --> 00:12:13,001
Who cares?

163
00:12:13,541 --> 00:12:16,461
It doesn't change the fact
that you'll get paid for killing him.

164
00:12:16,921 --> 00:12:19,881
Why do you think he didn't use one of his own men?

165
00:12:21,341 --> 00:12:24,221
Because that'd be going against orders.
He'd get his hands dirty.

166
00:12:24,301 --> 00:12:26,801
Well, that could be true.

167
00:12:27,971 --> 00:12:31,101
What if he's afraid of a loss?

168
00:12:31,601 --> 00:12:35,691
A loss so large that he won't
be able to explain it to his boss.

169
00:12:36,611 --> 00:12:39,361
An entire Jomsvikings unit?

170
00:12:39,441 --> 00:12:42,901
Just to get one washed-up soldier? That's crazy.

171
00:12:46,111 --> 00:12:48,911
Hey. Come down from there, kid.

172
00:12:51,291 --> 00:12:53,791
I want to get a look at this guy.

173
00:12:53,871 --> 00:12:55,461
"The Troll of Jom."

174
00:12:56,671 --> 00:13:00,381
I hope he's a fun guy.

175
00:13:19,561 --> 00:13:22,781
I can't even see the stars. I can't see anything.

176
00:13:22,861 --> 00:13:25,111
Which way are we heading?

177
00:13:26,201 --> 00:13:27,361
Thors.

178
00:13:27,741 --> 00:13:30,371
The wind changed a bit. Slightly to the right.

179
00:13:31,031 --> 00:13:33,661
I'll lead. Follow me.

180
00:13:33,751 --> 00:13:34,751
Got it.

181
00:13:41,961 --> 00:13:43,631
Amazing.

182
00:13:44,211 --> 00:13:48,131
How can Leif sail through the sea like this
without getting lost?

183
00:13:55,231 --> 00:13:56,101
Ari.

184
00:13:57,141 --> 00:13:59,151
Don't stare into the sea at night.

185
00:13:59,901 --> 00:14:01,401
It'll pull you in.

186
00:14:08,071 --> 00:14:09,661
Hey, Thors.

187
00:14:10,821 --> 00:14:13,161
What is it like on the battlefield?

188
00:14:15,041 --> 00:14:17,751
I heard you fought in a lot of battles.

189
00:14:18,541 --> 00:14:20,791
Tell us some stories.

190
00:14:21,671 --> 00:14:23,671
I want to cut off some general's head,

191
00:14:23,751 --> 00:14:25,171
so I can become a real man too.

192
00:14:29,051 --> 00:14:30,181
I see.

193
00:14:30,841 --> 00:14:34,181
My daughter likes strong men.

194
00:14:34,261 --> 00:14:35,931
You have a tough job ahead.

195
00:14:36,021 --> 00:14:38,891
Well, what can I say?

196
00:14:38,981 --> 00:14:40,191
You can tell?

197
00:14:41,351 --> 00:14:43,191
Are you in love with Ylva, Ari?

198
00:14:43,271 --> 00:14:46,191
Yeah, I like her. She's cute.

199
00:14:48,361 --> 00:14:52,991
She was born while I was still
in the Jomsvikings army.

200
00:14:53,531 --> 00:14:55,581
She was my first child.

201
00:15:04,921 --> 00:15:06,551
You're so loud.

202
00:15:06,631 --> 00:15:09,921
Do all babies cry so much?

203
00:15:10,011 --> 00:15:13,851
-Thors. Don't hold her like that.
-Her neck. Support her neck.

204
00:15:16,011 --> 00:15:18,351
Give me a boy next, Helga.

205
00:15:19,271 --> 00:15:21,351
The leader wants a boy.

206
00:15:22,401 --> 00:15:25,771
My wife Helga is the daughter of the leader
of the army.

207
00:15:26,821 --> 00:15:30,241
It was a difficult birth. She looked pale.

208
00:15:30,901 --> 00:15:31,911
Thors.

209
00:15:33,741 --> 00:15:35,621
Give her a name.

210
00:15:36,201 --> 00:15:37,621
Name her as you see fit.

211
00:15:38,201 --> 00:15:39,451
I'm busy.

212
00:15:39,871 --> 00:15:41,671
We're about to go on a campaign to Norway.

213
00:15:42,171 --> 00:15:44,131
Thors, the ship will soon depart.

214
00:15:44,211 --> 00:15:45,881
Okay. I'm coming.

215
00:15:45,961 --> 00:15:46,961
Thors.

216
00:15:51,171 --> 00:15:53,591
Give this child a name.

217
00:15:55,101 --> 00:15:57,561
I've been with her for 15 years,

218
00:15:58,011 --> 00:15:59,471
but that's the only time

219
00:15:59,721 --> 00:16:01,181
I've ever seen Helga mad.

220
00:16:07,151 --> 00:16:10,361
Ylva was my mother's name.

221
00:16:11,071 --> 00:16:12,861
It came to me all of a sudden.

222
00:16:13,861 --> 00:16:17,121
Now that I think about it, that's when it started.

223
00:16:18,621 --> 00:16:21,961
That's when I started to get scared of battle.

224
00:16:25,041 --> 00:16:26,631
That's why I ran away.

225
00:16:28,751 --> 00:16:33,011
I bet my old war buddies would curse me
if they knew.

226
00:16:36,761 --> 00:16:40,011
Hey. I can see the Faroe Islands.

227
00:16:58,531 --> 00:17:00,791
Father. Father.

228
00:17:00,871 --> 00:17:04,291
Are we in England? Did we arrive in England?

229
00:17:04,751 --> 00:17:07,041
No. Wrong answer.

230
00:17:07,501 --> 00:17:09,291
These are the Faroe Islands.

231
00:17:09,381 --> 00:17:12,341
They're in the middle, between Iceland and Norway.

232
00:17:12,421 --> 00:17:15,301
Our journey will be easier if we rest here for a bit.

233
00:17:15,801 --> 00:17:18,301
There's a village beyond this cove.

234
00:17:18,851 --> 00:17:21,971
Let's get some water there.
And we can trade too.

235
00:17:23,731 --> 00:17:26,901
Are you planning to come along,
all the way to England?

236
00:17:26,981 --> 00:17:27,811
Yeah.

237
00:17:29,271 --> 00:17:30,731
Get ready to row.

238
00:17:38,871 --> 00:17:40,331
Come on, hang in there.

239
00:17:42,621 --> 00:17:44,661
I wish we didn't have to do this.

240
00:17:44,751 --> 00:17:45,831
My butt hurts.

241
00:17:56,011 --> 00:17:57,971
What's wrong, Leif?

242
00:17:58,051 --> 00:17:59,221
Something's wrong.

243
00:17:59,721 --> 00:18:00,601
What's wrong?

244
00:18:01,141 --> 00:18:03,221
I wonder what's wrong.

245
00:18:04,181 --> 00:18:06,981
Something feels different
from the last time I was here.

246
00:18:16,361 --> 00:18:18,151
I see. It's the number of houses.

247
00:18:18,661 --> 00:18:20,491
The number of houses decreased.

248
00:18:21,531 --> 00:18:24,541
Let's turn back, Leif. I have a bad feeling about this.

249
00:18:24,991 --> 00:18:26,041
The terrain's bad too.

250
00:18:26,121 --> 00:18:28,161
What? Are you serious?

251
00:18:32,671 --> 00:18:35,591
Hey. They're going backwards.

252
00:18:35,671 --> 00:18:36,551
Did they notice us?

253
00:18:37,011 --> 00:18:38,381
They're good.

254
00:18:38,471 --> 00:18:41,051
They're very careful. They might be strong.

255
00:18:41,391 --> 00:18:43,761
They're too close, but it can't be helped.

256
00:18:43,851 --> 00:18:46,561
I don't care if the ships get damaged. Do it.

257
00:19:19,881 --> 00:19:21,591
Our exit...

258
00:19:22,681 --> 00:19:23,801
Take that.

259
00:19:23,891 --> 00:19:27,681
Great. They're caught like rats in a trap.

260
00:19:28,431 --> 00:19:31,191
Thors. Everyone. Are you okay?

261
00:19:31,271 --> 00:19:32,101
Is everyone okay?

262
00:19:32,521 --> 00:19:34,611
-Yes.
-We're okay.

263
00:19:35,151 --> 00:19:37,481
They will fire arrows.
Cover your head with your shield.

264
00:19:38,481 --> 00:19:40,321
Leif. How's the damage over there?

265
00:19:40,401 --> 00:19:42,991
We're okay. The ship is fine and everyone is okay.

266
00:19:47,291 --> 00:19:48,241
They're coming.

267
00:19:49,121 --> 00:19:52,461
Whoever's behind this trap
is in the back of the cove.

268
00:19:52,541 --> 00:19:53,501
The back?

269
00:20:09,271 --> 00:20:10,351
Pirates?

270
00:20:20,691 --> 00:20:22,901
These pillars are from a house.

271
00:20:22,991 --> 00:20:25,491
We're completely blocked.

272
00:20:25,571 --> 00:20:27,031
They got us.

273
00:20:27,121 --> 00:20:30,331
Maybe they'll spare our lives if we surrender.

274
00:20:30,411 --> 00:20:31,661
How do you know?

275
00:20:31,751 --> 00:20:33,081
They won't spare our lives.

276
00:20:33,161 --> 00:20:37,291
If they catch us, they'll sell us at the slave market.
Get ready.

277
00:20:37,381 --> 00:20:41,171
This is nothing.

278
00:20:42,511 --> 00:20:44,091
There's only two ships.

279
00:20:44,181 --> 00:20:45,431
Stop, Ari.

280
00:20:46,091 --> 00:20:47,551
They're experienced.

281
00:20:47,641 --> 00:20:51,431
They're not just some farmers working as pirates
in the summer for some extra cash.

282
00:20:51,721 --> 00:20:54,191
You're no match for them.

283
00:20:54,271 --> 00:20:56,481
Father...

284
00:21:08,241 --> 00:21:09,281
Thors...

285
00:21:22,421 --> 00:21:23,261
Thorfinn.

286
00:21:26,381 --> 00:21:29,891
Use it only to protect yourself. Understand?

287
00:21:29,971 --> 00:21:31,681
Only when you really need it.

288
00:21:39,481 --> 00:21:42,861
Are you going to kill them?
You are going to kill them.

289
00:21:44,901 --> 00:21:47,031
All right. I'm going to kill them.

290
00:21:47,111 --> 00:21:49,121
Stop saying "kill" so lightly.

291
00:21:56,461 --> 00:21:58,251
Bjorn. That mushroom...

292
00:21:59,251 --> 00:22:02,251
One, two, three...

293
00:22:02,341 --> 00:22:06,261
11, 12... And one kid?

294
00:22:06,761 --> 00:22:09,261
What? Is that all?

295
00:22:09,551 --> 00:22:11,721
Hey. Askeladd.

296
00:22:13,681 --> 00:22:16,141
Is it okay if I take care of them?

297
00:22:16,231 --> 00:22:19,191
It wouldn't be fun if all of us went after them at once.

298
00:22:19,271 --> 00:22:23,361
I'll go see
how good the Troll of Jom really is.

299
00:22:24,571 --> 00:22:27,531
Okay. They look like they want a fight too.

300
00:22:27,611 --> 00:22:28,451
What?

301
00:22:34,121 --> 00:22:36,411
-What?
-You bastard.

302
00:22:36,751 --> 00:22:38,291
What's wrong with you?

303
00:22:38,661 --> 00:22:40,751
Where did you come from?

304
00:22:44,381 --> 00:22:45,211
Brother.

305
00:22:46,631 --> 00:22:47,721
He's good.

306
00:22:47,921 --> 00:22:49,221
Take this.

307
00:23:06,111 --> 00:23:07,491
You're good...

308
00:23:09,241 --> 00:23:11,071
Troll of Jom.
